WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:03.140
What the hell is that bastard
Makusu thinking?!

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.940
Can people really be so dense?

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.940
Besides, isn't Cecilcchi
directly involved with the case?

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.020
Is she even allowed to defend him?

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:16.240
Makusu personally selected her,
so the court can't oppose it.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.990
But this will be too much
for Cecil to handle.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.140
What's he planning?

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.510
We've learned that something which
was originally white is actually black.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.780
I don't think she should do it.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.510
I agree.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:34.270
Right?! Not to mention he had the nerve
to ask Butterfly to defend him.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.490
You think you've seen it all,

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:34.890
but the truth remains shrouded
further inside the black.

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.530
So pissed off!

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.390
Flip it again,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.050
Makusu's totally mocking us!

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.170
and it becomes white.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.760
What do you want to do, Cecil?

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.930
Why don't you go meet him?

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:53.940
If you're this uncertain, then you only need to
see him so that you can make your decision.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.190
...Natcchi...

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.830
Um, is that all right?

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.450
Of course. Let's do that.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:04.950
...All right, Hachimitsu and Hotaru...

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.450
I'm counting on you.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.460
Yes, ma'am.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:14.790
But still, Hotarin's been
awfully nice to Cecilcchi lately.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:19.560
Fact or Fiction

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:19.560
Case 12

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:15.990
Up until now,
she'd have yelled at her,

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.720
saying "It's your job,
so you can't choose".

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.850
It's a good thing that Natcchi
is being nice to Cecilun!

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.490
...But...

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:26.690
...Natcchi getting close to Cecil is...

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:27.940
Unforgivable!

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:32.950
Cecilun!

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.950
What's with you?

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.450
We heard you're keeping quiet.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.380
Will you speak to us?

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.960
Sudou is the one I asked for.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.210
I'd like to speak to her alone.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:50.710
...U-Um...

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.220
I did something terrible to you.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.160
...I was under the influence of Lucifer...

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.310
I wanted to punish the humans
for discriminating against Wuds,

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.850
and create a world only for Wuds.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.620
But in the end, I lost everything

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.810
due to this foolish ambition.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.850
My status, my honor,

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.600
and even my son.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:15.950
<i>His son?</i>

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.040
I'll confess everything
at the Court for Magic.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:25.970
Huh?

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:28.670
I'll reveal my motive then.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.210
And I'll admit to everything,
starting with the incident six years ago.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.840
R-Really?

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.590
So you'll speak for my mom?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:40.610
While Sudou Megumi
<i>did use magic to protect you,</i>

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:44.480
that wasn't what killed Inspector Oda.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:49.230
So you killed him?

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:57.150
If you're going to admit to this,
then at least show me the evidence.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.570
...Otherwise...

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.160
I asked you to represent me
as a way of making amends.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.330
You said so yourself.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.840
That I should confess everything
in the Court for Magic.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.090
I don't think there's any other way.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.270
I've investigated a lot into
...what happened six years ago...

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.220
But I can't find any evidence.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.670
If it's possible to shed
any light on that case,

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.930
then I think I should accept.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.230
Do you think he'll really come clean?

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:34.490
I kinda doubt it, given his history.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:36.650
That may be.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.170
Ordinary methods won't work on him.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.870
...Yes, I know...

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:45.470
But this could be my chance
to get my mom a retrial.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.490
So I want to do everything I can.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.270
...Well, when you put it that way...

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.880
We'll do what we can.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.470
We'll have to devise a plan
to make sure he testifies.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.750
He's different from
any of your previous clients.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.430
We need to be very cautious.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.510
If I can be of any help,
feel free to ask.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.650
...Thank you very much...

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:18.020
I'll be counting on you.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.020
...On that day, six years ago...

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:26.290
By the time we got you to
...the hospital, you were already...

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.220
Cecil!

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:37.430
A man spoke to me.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:42.730
He said he could bring you
back to life using summoning magic.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:45.930
I was confused at first.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:51.460
I didn't care if it was a forbidden spell.
I just wanted you back.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.130
...But...

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:55.440
It was just a trap from the get-go.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.570
To make Lucifer notice your existence,

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:03.270
they needed to send your soul
into the Demon World.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.810
So that's why my memories are fuzzy.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:06.770
Yeah.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:10.180
It was all so Makusu
could get his hands on you.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:15.520
He was using you by awakening your
magical powers in an attempt to lure Lucifer

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.650
into this world with
summoning magic.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.310
Those revived with summoning magic
could lose control of their magic.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.550
That's why I sent you
all those hair accessories.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.210
Those stones are talismans
to suppress your magic.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.170
...I'm sorry I'm such an unreliable father...

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:37.280
...I couldn't protect you or your mother...

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.780
<i>I have to expose the truth.</i>

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:47.550
Wait, I have to control myself tonight!

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:05.900
I'm Katase Masayoshi,
the prosecutor on this case.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.680
I hear you recently tried to see me,

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.640
Sudou Cecil.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:11.850
Yes.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.590
We'll get to what you wanted later.

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:19.650
For now, I look forward
to being in court with you.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.410
A pleasure.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.720
Who's that?

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.870
He was the prosecutor
at my mother's trial.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:26.660
Huh?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:31.910
We shall now begin
the preliminary hearing.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:37.400
This is an unusual case, as someone
involved is representing the defendant.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.420
I have no objections.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:44.850
Well then, let the prosecution and defense
present their opening arguments.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.430
The suspect, Makusu Shimon,

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:53.680
is charged with violating magic-prohibition law,
articles 1 and 9 for creating a metamoloid,

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.410
and with destruction of property.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:01.320
But regarding if he should be charged
using article 5, not declaring he's a wizard,

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:05.950
and article 6, holding a
...governmental position as a wizard...

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.740
I withdraw all charges.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:08.820
Huh?

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.020
Why?

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:15.120
I believe the defendant's outstanding service
as a judge is reasonable grounds

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.150
to grant him special consideration.

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.080
...But...

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:26.430
Shouldn't the defendant's relationship
to the law weigh heavily in favor of conviction?

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:30.070
That's even more reason
not to indict him.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.230
The suspect has been discharged.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:35.270
I believe that a simple fine
is more than enough.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:38.270
It'll also ensure a speedy trial.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.480
The court accepts the
withdrawal of charges.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.880
Also, the defendant has applied for bail.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.870
He doesn't pose a flight risk,

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:51.620
so I won't oppose it.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.120
The prosecutor from six years ago, huh?

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.120
Butterfly Law Offices

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.730
So Makusu is plotting
something, after all.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:03.290
He probably has no plans to confess
what happened six years ago.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:07.380
It might be time for
the ace up our sleeve.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.880
Let's go fully prepared.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:13.640
...I'm sorry for calling you out here...

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:17.770
Thank you so much for
protecting me all this time.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:18.510
It's fine.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.520
Actually, I believe we contributed
to a strange misunderstanding.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.400
Sorry about that.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.660
...Um...

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:29.660
Do you know of any evidence that'd shed light on
Director Makusu and Prosecutor Katase's relationship?

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.590
We're not aware of any personal matters.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.110
I see.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:36.290
If I can't prove that they're in cahoots,

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:40.570
then I'll have to find evidence that
I was subject to summoning magic.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:41.870
What do you mean?

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:46.530
I've already given a statement to the
police about the summoning magic,

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.540
but they didn't believe me.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:53.250
I didn't regain consciousness
until the summoning had failed.

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:54.550
I see.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:09:00.020
I need evidence of any kind to
force Makusu to testify at trial.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.940
...If we only had Grimoire 365...

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:09.340
That's the book I mentioned that has
Wud history and prophecy written in it.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:13.160
They probably used it
during the summoning.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:14.670
Any ideas?

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:15.910
...No...

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:20.410
When the summoning failed, it may have been destroyed.

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:27.170
The police confiscated the evidence.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:31.420
Yeah, but I need a lead of
some sort. Anything will do.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:42.230
How are your wounds?

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:43.700
...Better, for the most part...

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:44.730
...That charm...

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.290
Isn't that the one Shizumu had?

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:47.020
Eh?

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:52.150
I heard you were with
Shizumu when he died.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:53.370
...Yes...

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:57.430
Talking about it has become
a taboo within the precinct.

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:59.780
Damn them all.

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.670
Make sure the truth comes out.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.610
For his sake, as well.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:11.720
Get Rid of
\hthe Wuds!

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:19.650
Former Supreme Court Chief Justice
Makusu Shimon's trial

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:22.080
is about to start at the Court for Magic.

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:28.860
...I couldn't find anything...

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.800
...Grimoire 365...

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:34.110
Here.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:38.410
Thank you.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:42.670
By the way, this is the first case
we've worked together on, isn't it?

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:43.410
Yeah.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:47.330
The world's watching,
so make sure you keep up.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:51.090
Yeah... I need to make this count.

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:54.920
This case will only have
meaning if I do my job.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.810
That's rather conceited.

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:58.650
I think so too.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:00.430
But I agree.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:04.180
You <i>are the right person for the job.</i>

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:10.070
I'll do everything I can to help you.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:12.940
Thank you.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:20.450
We'll now begin the trial.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.580
Let me ask you this.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:30.080
On the night of the incident, the barrister Sudou Cecil
was present at your Akasaka apartment.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.550
Why is that?

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:35.840
According to what she told the police,

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:42.600
you kidnapped Sudou Cecil to call the
demon Lucifer using summoning magic.

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:45.350
Do you disagree with this?

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:50.550
However, in the end,
the summoning failed.

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:53.860
So you created a metamoloid,
and tried to kill her.

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:55.860
Do you disagree with this?

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:01.370
I cannot use summoning magic.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.660
That is the counsel's mere delusion.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.530
Delusion?

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:11.420
It is true that the counselor
was at my apartment,

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:14.830
but she appeared to be unconscious.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.880
So you're saying her
testimony isn't credible?

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:18.670
Yes.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:22.550
The prosecution mentioned
that you created a metamoloid.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:25.290
What was your motive behind that?

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:30.810
You were angered by the
summoning spell's failure,

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.810
so you created the metamoloid.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:33.810
Is that incorrect?

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:39.050
Because the ritual that can only be
performed once every hundred years had failed,

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:40.570
you were blind with rage.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:44.510
In fact, you created a metamoloid
in the heat of the moment,

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:46.080
without premeditation.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:47.710
Correct?

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:52.580
As I stated earlier,
summoning magic doesn't exist.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.330
It's a mere delusion.

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.860
So he really <i>does intend to play dumb.</i>

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:01.000
It's just as we thought.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:01.980
Let's go.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.290
According to counsel's testimony,

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:09.850
you killed your son, Mr. Shizumu,
who was a police officer.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.730
Is this true?

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:18.730
You just stated that the counselor's testimony
wasn't credible because she was unconscious.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.990
Can anyone else confirm this?

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:28.050
After this incident, the defendant
created a metamoloid.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:31.370
Was this related to your son's death?

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.250
No further questions.

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:35.550
I'd like to change the topic.

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:40.150
How much knowledge do you
have of summoning magic?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.900
How about Lucifer?

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:43.750
None.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:47.890
When you had created your
metamoloid and fought against me,

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:53.020
do you not remember saying you'd punish the
humans that had discriminated against Wuds?

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:58.430
That's why you needed to summon
Lucifer and used me as a catalyst.

00:13:58.430 --> 00:13:59.900
Objection!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:05.910
The counsel's testimony is a
personal impression, lacking objectivity.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:07.680
Objection sustained.

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:12.400
I just want the court to be fully aware
of the facts before passing a judgment!

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:15.930
The counselor's statement
wasn't that of a wizard barrister.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:18.550
Rather, it's just a
personal victim statement.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:22.110
Without other witnesses,
it isn't valid evidence.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.920
If we go by the suspect's testimony,

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:27.150
the counselor shouldn't have
any recollection of what happened.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:31.180
That casts real doubt on her credibility.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:35.190
I request more objective
evidence and testimony.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.080
He's objecting to a statement
that would benefit the prosecution!

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.450
There's no time! Hurry and get in!

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:50.630
Do you feel like telling the court what
happened at your apartment in Akasaka?

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:54.030
Was your son involved at all?

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:57.580
I'll tell the defense everything.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:01.880
Does that mean you're
willing to admit that

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:05.010
this case is related to
...the one six years ag—

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:07.220
Summoning magic does not exist.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:09.180
...So...

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:16.310
I created the metamoloid and attacked the
counselor because Sudou Cecil killed my son!

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.060
What do you mean?

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:25.070
The counselor knew my son was a wizard.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.170
She threatened Shizumu,

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:31.070
saying she'd expose him as a wizard
unless he found something

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:32.950
that'd allow a retrial for her mother.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.330
But my son refused to give in.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:37.580
So she killed him.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:38.960
N-No way!

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:42.760
I was enraged by the
death of my beloved son.

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:45.630
So I created a metamoloid
and attacked her.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:47.210
Th-That isn't true!

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:49.770
Shizumu died trying to save me!

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:51.090
<i>You're the one who killed Shizumu!</i>

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.850
...I couldn't forgive the counselor...

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:55.970
I couldn't forgive
Sudou Cecil for killing my son!

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.490
That was my motive!

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:01.730
I believe a trial regarding counsel's violation
of the magic-prohibition law's article 1,

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.980
as well as murder, is necessary.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:07.490
No! Director Makusu was
the one who killed Shizumu!

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:08.990
But you have no proof.

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:13.490
The only ones at the scene were you,
the defendant, and the victim.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:18.120
That means one of you
is lying to the court!

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.450
You can't be serious!

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.890
There's no way that Cecil
would do a thing like that!

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:24.300
Hotaru, calm down.
Don't get emotional.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.000
...But...

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:29.830
I wanted to make my statement in the
presence of those that uphold the law.

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:32.760
That's why I said nothing before the trial.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:39.350
Your Honor, I would like to call Sudou Cecil
to the stand as a witness in this case.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:42.770
Very well.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:43.610
Huh?

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:45.190
...But...

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:50.450
Please wait a moment!

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:55.080
I've brought a witness.

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.120
Ageha!

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:06.800
Huh?

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:08.090
Shindaiji!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.460
But how?

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.030
He was the ace up our sleeve.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:14.490
This is your chance to expose
the truth about six years ago.

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:15.350
Do your best.

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:17.350
Okay!

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:18.610
Your Honor!

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:20.530
Reviewing the witnesses
...prior to trial is required—

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:24.830
For the sake of learning the truth,
I will allow this exception.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:31.740
This case is connected to a
certain incident six years ago.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:35.740
It was made to look like Inspector Oda
accidentally killed Sudou Cecil.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.150
And with Inspector Oda dead,
he couldn't say otherwise.

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:43.470
Makusu then proposed to me that her mother,
Sudou Megumi, take the blame.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.380
Along with Prosecutor Katase
and the wizard barrister Yabe,

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:50.750
we proceeded with a trial to ensure that
Sudou Megumi would be found guilty.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:54.850
I know that it was an act
unbefitting of a judge.

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:56.890
...And I...

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:59.390
I was almost killed by this man!

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:06.520
Defendant, is any of this
familiar to you?

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:08.020
It is not.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:11.280
Shindaiji's testimony lacks objectivity.

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:15.730
I believe his testimony could be
used to entrap the defendant,

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:17.790
and does not count as evidence.

00:18:17.790 --> 00:18:19.910
Katase, you may say that,

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.290
but even you were in on this!

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:23.910
...Th-There's no proof...

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.170
Exactly!

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.170
It's as the prosecution says.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:30.420
There's no evidence in either
this case or the one six years ago!

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:32.550
You said you would tell the truth!

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.630
You need evidence, Sudou.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:38.680
If only you had solid evidence
of this summoning magic.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.110
Evidence.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:47.080
...<i>Think... There has to be something...</i>

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:49.440
<i>Evidence... Evidence!</i>

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:52.440
...<i>Remember, Cecil...</i>

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:53.930
...Evidence...

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:57.190
Calm down, Cecil.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.150
Wh-What is this?

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:05.770
Huh?

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:08.710
Cecil!

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.370
Cecil, that's it!

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.250
That's Grimoire 365!

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.130
...Shizumu...

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.640
Damn you and your
interference, Shizumu.

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:21.010
Wud history and prophecy
is written here.

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:25.650
I submit this as evidence in both the
case six years ago and our current case!

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.540
Th-That doesn't count as evidence!

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:32.270
Everything concerning the
ritual and me is written in here!

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:36.490
The magical cuffs were rigged!

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:40.690
You little pests aren't
worthy of judging me!

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.420
Die, Sudou Cecil!

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:00.550
Cecil!

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:02.850
That's enough, Makusu!

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.390
Now!

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:06.890
Yeah!

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.490
Your Honor!

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:19.450
We shall temporarily suspend this case.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:22.370
Restrain Makusu Shimon!

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:23.370
What?

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:33.710
Stop!

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:44.310
How could I, Makusu Shimon,

00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:47.310
be sent to the maritime prison?

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:05.910
We won't consider what you just did
a violation of the Magic Prohibition Act.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.830
Thank you!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.410
You're still wearing your cosplay outfit,

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.540
but you've come a long way.

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:16.330
Thank you very much, Your Honor!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.930
Ageha, nice timing!

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:22.750
That was pretty impressive,
if I do say so myself.

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:25.800
But the real hero here is Sasori.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:34.440
It's only because Sasorin used precog to do
a reading that we were able to save Shindaiji.

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:37.120
Thank goodness he listened to me.

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:39.710
It went pretty well with the judge, too.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:42.970
So maybe you can get
your mother a retrial.

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:43.820
Yeah!

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:47.210
Thank you,

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:48.450
Natcchi!

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:49.650
Huh?

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:53.050
I... I didn't do anything.

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:58.840
Higher up.

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:01.320
I'm sure it was somewhere around here.

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:02.090
There it is!

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:04.340
Something good happened.

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:04.380
May the death sentence not happen!

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:04.380
May Mom get a retrial!

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:04.380
Cecil

00:22:07.600 --> 00:22:09.600
Butterfly Law Offices

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.600
Cecilun!

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:12.940
Cecilun, there's trouble!
Trouble! Trouble!

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:14.980
We got an insane case!

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:17.390
It's the first big one in a long time.

00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:19.610
This will be a good test of our skills.

00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:20.850
All right!

00:22:20.850 --> 00:22:24.990
Time to make the police's batons
seem totally impotent.

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:27.870
Stop moving like that in front of Cecilcchi.

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:30.030
So, how do we want to
decide the teams?

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:32.620
How about making Cecil the captain?

00:22:32.620 --> 00:22:33.530
Huh?

00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:38.380
After Cecil and Hotaru
gain more experience.

00:22:38.780 --> 00:22:41.130
Let's give this case our all.

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:42.880
I won't lose to you.

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:44.310
Likewise.

00:22:45.880 --> 00:22:48.010
Get even more fired-up!

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:50.810
Don't egg them on.

00:22:50.810 --> 00:22:54.010
I love Hotaru when she's more angry.

00:22:54.010 --> 00:22:56.390
...She's being too friendly with Cecil...

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:58.870
The world isn't that nice.

00:22:58.870 --> 00:23:02.650
You've still have a ways to go, Cecil!

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:05.610
You don't have to tell me twice.

00:23:09.840 --> 00:23:11.490
Oh no! I'm late again!

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:13.790
...It's Sunday, Cecilun...

00:23:21.590 --> 00:23:24.300
I've been meaning to
ask you this for a while now.

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:25.300
What is it?

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.810
Just who are you, Moyoyon?

00:23:28.390 --> 00:23:30.720
I had a strange dream the other day.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:31.970
Promise not to tell?

00:23:32.740 --> 00:23:34.680
...I'm...
